# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# Why this file exists: the whole point of moving off pinned jsDelivr tags is
# that a push goes live WITHOUT editing the Webflow footer. That only works if
# browsers don't sit on a stale copy. jsDelivr's default for an unpinned URL is
# max-age=604800 (7 days in the browser) — which is why @main was never a real
# option.
#
# max-age=0 + must-revalidate means the browser asks "changed?" on every load
# and gets a tiny 304 when it hasn't. Updates are effectively instant; the cost
# is one conditional request per file (HTTP/2 multiplexed, negligible).
#
# If you later want fewer round-trips and can live with a short delay, change
# max-age=0 to max-age=60. Do NOT raise it much beyond that without going back
# to pinned versions — long cache + floating URL is how you ship a fix nobody
# receives.

/src/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
